🚽 Test case: #196 -- a struct/union pointer-typed FUNCTION PARAMETER
🚽 rejects a non-struct argument, not just a wrong-tag struct argument
🚽 (PR #248 review, round 3, finding 2). check_pointer_struct_tag_match()
🚽 alone fail-opens on an argument whose struct tag it cannot determine
🚽 -- correct for a genuinely unknown expression, but `&n` for a plain
🚽 `rizz n` is DEFINITELY not a struct at all (empty struct_name, same as
🚽 "unknown"), and the call-argument check had no separate category
🚽 check the way declaration/assignment already do via
🚽 check_type_compatibility_ex().
gang Point {
    rizz x;
    rizz y;
};

skibidi bump(gang Point *pp) {
    pp.x = 99;
}

skibidi main {
    rizz n;
    n = 42;
    bump(&n);
    yapping("%d", n);
}
